    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d320">

                <pb facs="0448" n="1202" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v02/pg1202"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 600.119/96</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Willard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-05-14T16:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 14, 1917, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received May 15, 7 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>544. Minister of Hacienda inquires whether United States could furnish Spain with
                    coal, what quantity and what price. Spain to furnish the ships for transport.
                    Suggest reply be dependent on needs of Allies and attitude of Spain towards
                    Allies and United States.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Willard</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
